Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:12:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] android: remove the Waydroid runtime and `bonk waydroid`
 command

Project owner's decision (2026-11-10): LynxDroid must not depend on
Waydroid. This removes it from the engine instead of leaving it as the
selected runtime.

Removed:
- waydroid_runtime.{hpp,cpp} and its unit tests
- the `bonk waydroid` CLI command with its --waydroid, --confirm-start,
  --show-ui, --install-apk, --confirm-install-apk and --launch-package
  options (main.cpp, cli.cpp, cli.hpp, cli_test.cpp and the Makefile are
  back to their state at fa22179, the last commit before Waydroid)
- tests/waydroid_cli_test.sh and the `waydroid-cli-test` make target
- the Waydroid host runbook in docs/ANDROID_ENGINE.md

Kept, made backend-neutral:
- engine_state and launcher_plan only depended on Waydroid through two
  type names. They now use RuntimeState / RuntimeStatus from the new
  runtime_status.hpp, so the layered snapshot and the launcher-plan
  contract and all of their tests survive.
- error codes android.waydroid_start_consent_required and
  android.waydroid_state_unknown are renamed to
  android.runtime_start_consent_required and
  android.runtime_state_unknown.

Untouched: EngineSession, the SDK Emulator/AVD command builder,
preflight, adb_client, input_action.

Consequence, stated plainly in the docs: no runtime backend is selected
and nothing in the tree starts Android. plan_launcher() and
render_engine_snapshot() are library code with unit tests and no caller.

A new test, cli.has_no_waydroid_command_or_options, fails if the command
or any of its options comes back.

make -j2 verify: 364 tests, 0 failed (was 377; the 14 removed tests
covered only the Waydroid adapter and CLI, one test was added).

